1
00:05:09,473 --> 00:05:15,473
A Motion Picture with a stirring message on Marriage! A
Powerful Film, full of truths of life and love!

2
00:10:18,947 --> 00:10:24,947
The Crowd is a drama, romance film directed by King Vidor.

3
00:15:28,421 --> 00:15:34,421
John, an ambitious but undisciplined New York City
office worker, meets and marries Mary.

4
00:20:37,894 --> 00:20:43,894
They start a family, struggle to cope with marital stress, financial setbacks, and
tragedy, all while lost amid the anonymous, pitiless throngs of the big city.

5
00:25:47,368 --> 00:25:53,368
Mary Sims, played by Eleanor Boardman.

6
00:30:56,842 --> 00:31:02,842
John 'Johnny' Sims, played by James Murray.

7
00:36:06,315 --> 00:36:12,315
Bert, played by Bert Roach.

8
00:41:15,789 --> 00:41:21,789
Jane, played by Estelle Clark.

9
00:46:25,263 --> 00:46:31,263
Jim, played by Daniel G. Tomlinson.

10
00:51:34,736 --> 00:51:40,736
Dick, played by Dell Henderson.

11
00:56:44,210 --> 00:56:50,210
The Crowd is a 1928 American silent drama film directed by King Vidor and
starring James Murray, Eleanor Boardman and Bert Roach.

12
01:01:53,684 --> 01:01:59,684
The feature film was nominated at the first Academy Award presentation in 1929 for several
awards, including Unique and Artistic Production for MGM and Best Director for Vidor.

13
01:07:03,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Kevin Brownlow and David Gill restored The Crowd in 1981, and
it was released with a score by Carl Davis.

14
01:12:12,631 --> 01:12:18,631
In 1989, the film was one of the first 25 selected by the Library of Congress for preservation in the United
States National Film Registry for being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

15
01:17:22,105 --> 01:17:28,105
In February 2020, the film was shown at the 70th Berlin International Film
Festival, as part of a retrospective dedicated to Vidor's career.

16
01:22:31,578 --> 01:22:37,578
The film entered the public domain in the United States in 2024.

17
01:27:41,052 --> 01:27:47,052
The film explores themes of new york city, marriage, tragedy, silent film.

18
01:32:50,526 --> 01:32:56,526
The tone is emotional.
